# Code owners for sera-agents.
#
# CODEOWNERS only *requests* review by itself. To make it binding, enable
# branch protection on `main` with "Require a pull request before merging" +
# "Require review from Code Owners" (see SECURITY.md § CI/CD supply chain).
#
# The CI paths below are deliberately the tightest: a workflow file can read
# every secret the repository can see, so changes there must be reviewed by an
# admin. This path was the vector for the 2026-09-05 credential-exfiltration
# incident, which reached `main` as a direct push with no review.

# Default — any change gets admin review.
*                       @douglasgan @dev-sera

# CI / CD and anything that can execute with repository secrets.
/.github/               @douglasgan @dev-sera
/.github/workflows/     @douglasgan @dev-sera

# Deployment + edge configuration (TLS, ingress, container topology).
/docker-compose.yml     @douglasgan @dev-sera
/Dockerfile             @douglasgan @dev-sera
/agents-gateway/deploy/ @douglasgan @dev-sera

# Anything that touches keys, payments, or the published security posture.
/x402-service/          @douglasgan @dev-sera
/SECURITY.md            @douglasgan @dev-sera
/SECURITY-MODEL.md      @douglasgan @dev-sera
